            <ArticleTitle>Common presentation uncommon diagnosis primary omental torsion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>117-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary omental torsion is a rare cause of acute abdomen and mimics common acute abdominal condition like appendicitis. Torsion of the greater omentum may be primary or secondary. Here we present 2 cases admitted through emergency with the pain in right iliac fossa with this unusual diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
